{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI write from Paris, where I arrived this morning. The heat is oppressive, and the city feels like a living beast, breathing in the streets. I have secured a room at the Hôtel des Princes, a respectable establishment, though the dust is already settling on my coat.\n\nI paid my respects to Cousin immediately; he is still vigorous, if somewhat lost in his own system. I spent the afternoon wandering the Boulevards and the Palais Royal. The crowds are immense, a chaotic mix of commerce and idleness. I walked the Champs Élysées this evening, past the cafés and carousels, where families gather in the fading light. It is a spectacle of pure sensuous life, lacking the quiet dignity I find in our home. I miss the silence of Berlin and the comfort of your company. Pray tell the boys their father thinks of them.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219235,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":197,"prompt_tokens":956,"total_tokens":1153,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-8XVZaUc4TnWSzTIyts5z3g1xdDXQ0GcH","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":956,"prompt_ms":893.719,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9348525104602511,"prompt_per_second":1069.6874520962403,"predicted_n":197,"predicted_ms":4624.263,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.59317857142857,"predicted_per_second":42.3851325065205}}